  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1212 AM MDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nWill keep this long term discussion short a sweet as there is not \nmuch to talk about with the synoptic set-up that will take hold over \nthe region. Starting off the long term period, Friday marks the day \nthat ridging takes hold. This will not only usher in warmer \ntemperatures, but block or hamper any moisture transport into the \nregion, resulting in an increased risk of critical and/or elevated \nfire weather conditions, more on that in a bit. Therefore, expect \ndry conditions with highs topping out well into the 90s by Friday. \nThen the real heat makes a return over the weekend when highs once \nagain surge into the low 100s, warmest across far eastern Wyoming \nand the Nebraska Panhandle. As mentioned briefly, with the ridge \nstrengthening, don't expect much relief from any precipitation as we \nwill remain dry heading into next week. A byproduct of this dryness \nand heat will be an increase in fire weather concerns as daytime RH \nvalues plummet into the single digit to teens each day. Because of \nthis, expect an elevated fire weather environment, with the \npotential to become critical with any increase in winds. So stay \ntuned...",
